<package packagerversion="1.10.0" version="2.0" xmlns="http://pear.php.net/dtd/package-2.0" xmlns:tasks="http://pear.php.net/dtd/tasks-1.0" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://pear.php.net/dtd/tasks-1.0 http://pear.php.net/dtd/tasks-1.0.xsd http://pear.php.net/dtd/package-2.0 http://pear.php.net/dtd/package-2.0.xsd">
 <name>scope</name>
 <channel>pecl.php.net</channel>
 <summary>Scope: the identity of the operation (request, job) that code belongs to</summary>
 <description>The Scope class proposed in the PHP RFC "Scope", for PHP 8.2 and later. Fibers and generators belong to the scope current at their creation; Scope::getRootScope() is the scope outside any Scope::run().</description>
 <lead>
  <name>Frode Børli</name>
  <user>frodeborli</user>
  <email>frode@ennerd.com</email>
  <active>yes</active>
 </lead>
 <date>2026-10-19</date>
 <version>
  <release>0.3.0</release>
  <api>0.3.0</api>
 </version>
 <stability>
  <release>alpha</release>
  <api>alpha</api>
 </stability>
 <license uri="https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT">MIT</license>
 <notes>Scope spec level 0.3.0: the RFC draft plus secondary votes A (per-scope request superglobals, ini scope.superglobals) and B (per-scope default timezone and locale, ini scope.locale_timezone). Includes Scope with getRootScope(), getCurrent(), run(); Fiber::getScope() and Generator::getScope().</notes>
